    <string name="how_it_works">How is this calculated?</string>
    <string name="how_it_works_text">• Solar energy used at home avoids buying it from the grid, so it saves its price per kWh. The price comes from your bill for that month (amount minus fixed charges, divided by the kWh bought), or from the default in Settings.\n\n• Energy sent to the grid earns the feed-in price. When neither the bill nor the inverter says how much was exported, it is estimated from the self-consumption percentage.\n\n• Energy stored in a battery and used later counts as self-consumed.\n\n• Payback: the yearly savings (last 12 months, or an extrapolation) are projected into the future with the expected price increase and panel degradation, until they cover the total investment, including extras like a battery.</string>

